// divzero_no_rt.tk -- D82 ruling 5: the guard `tk_div_guard` builds calls
// `panic` (`lib/rt.tk`), which is program code and not something every unit
// carries. A division the folder cannot see through, in a program that
// never included the runtime, is refused BY NAME where it is written --
// rather than compiling into a call mc then refuses as "call to unknown
// function: panic".
//
// A program with no division that needs a guard is untouched: `tests/
// hello.tk` includes nothing at all and compiles.
//
// expect-refuse: teko: an integer division needs #include rt.tk
// expect-refuse-line: 17

i64 main() {
    i64 n = 0;
    i64 a = 10;
    i64 q = a / n;
    if (q == 0) return 1;
    return 42;
}
